<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Vasates</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Cossium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aquitanian people south of the Garonne whose town Cossium became Bazas, centre of the Bazadais.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Vasates, called Vocates by Caesar, lived south of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gironde">Gironde</a>. They surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 56 BCE with the other Aquitanian peoples.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>No rulers or institutions are known. Their territory lay between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> valley and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landes-forest">Landes forest</a>, on the route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Burdigala</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bazas">Cossium</a> was renamed Civitas Vasatica, from which comes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baza">Bazas</a>. The poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ausonius">Ausonius</a> had family links with the town, and its district kept the name Bazadais.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:4.86%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cossium</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vocates</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=vasates" aria-label="Vasates on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4740 504 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vasates lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5060 760h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5060 760h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=vasates">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

